{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Business Requirements and the Functional Requirements"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you are discussing business and functional requirements. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Make the coding of the system modules and the main program, starting from using the chosen programming language, based on design specifications.   Exchanges information about requirements types and their characteristics."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the graphic layout of an IT solution, functional requirements of a business through the IT solution, and the functional phase of an IT project."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine that you are the manager of a company and you have to deal with a difficult process."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about how to reduce the time that staff spends in that process."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write the procedure and describe the steps."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write an email to a software company with the functional and business requirements. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with your partner."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information about actions plans to reduce time in procedures. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write and describe procedures."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about functional and business company requirements."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Questions With How + Adjective?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Using <span class =\"strong\">adjectives</span> within how questions helps a lot when you want to inquire about specific characteristics of an element or a person."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>The inclusion of&nbsp;<strong>adjectives</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>within the &ldquo;<i>how questions</i>&rdquo; helps you find out the attributes as well as the characteristics that a person or an object has. By asking these questions, you can get to know someone or something very well.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> You can follow different structures in order to create different types of <strong>how + adjective</strong> questions:&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">How + adjective + is/are + noun?</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong><i>How different are</i></strong><i> those two requirements you just mentioned?<br /> <br /> </i></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">How + adjective + can + subject + verb + complement?&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong><i>How easy can</i></strong><i> we create software?</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><br /> How + adjective + do/does + subject + verb?</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong><i>How often do</i></strong><i> we address the necessity for meeting the business goals?</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How bad is the stock problem of the company?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Okay, how grueling is it to do all of that?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Business and Functional Requirements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Within a system, there are various and different requirements that work together to make that system function. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">BUSINESS REQUIREMENTS </span> </br> The business requirements are the starting point of any system. These requirements are identified by analyzing the problems or flaws of the business which are then expressed as the goals or objectives that the system will intend to meet and achieve. All business requirements must be clear but have to contain enough information in order to ensure an effective impact on the addressed problem once the system is developed. </br> </br>  <span class =\"strong\">FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS </span> </br> Remember that functional requirements describe the different processes of systems represented in terms of input and output. That is the behavior of the system in different situations. Its writing is characterized by the use of verbs that explicitly define the work that the system must perform."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stock"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the amount of products available for customers to buy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How bad is the stock problem of the company?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ASAP"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "acronym for  \u201cas soon as possible\u201d"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, we really need to find a solution ASAP."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "arise"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to occur, happen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Otherwise, economic loss will arise and we will definitely be in trouble."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grueling"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "difficult, hard to achieve"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Okay, how grueling is it to do all of that?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "proceed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to continue with the next action or phase"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Once we analyze the general situation of the company and determine the objective or vision for the system, we are ready to proceed with the next step. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "all in all"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "expression used to conclude an idea, equivalent to \u201cto sum up\u201d"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: All in all, they reflect the way the necessity for meeting the business goals is going to be addressed. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe what the business requirements refer to."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the relationship between functional requirements and the business requirements."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you consider that software eases chores for companies? Why? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are some of the most common problems that companies face in general? List some of them. "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "conte