ective or vision for the system, we are ready to proceed with the next step.</br></br>"}, {"time": "42000", "image": "", "id": 5, "text": "<strong>George:</strong> What is the next step going to be?</br></br>"}, {"time": "44000", "image": "", "id": 6, "text": "<strong>Juliana:</strong> We continue with the development of the functional requirements which basically describe the processes of the system in terms of input and output. In other words, we designate the behavior of the system in different situations and the way it is going to respond to the company's issues. All in all, they reflect the way the necessity for meeting the business goals is going to be addressed.</br></br>"}, {"time": "66000", "image": "", "id": 7, "text": "<strong>George:</strong> How different are those two requirements you just mentioned?</br></br>"}, {"time": "69000", "image": "", "id": 8, "text": "<strong>Juliana:</strong> They are closer than you think. The business requirements are the starting point of any system and the functional requirements are based on them. Furthermore, behind any system, there is a necessity for meeting the business requirements.</br></br>"}, {"time": "82500", "image": "", "id": 9, "text": "<strong>George:</strong> Perfect, we are calling a software company right away, then.</br></br>"}, {"time": "85800", "image": "", "id": 10, "text": "<strong>Juliana:</strong> Yes, we meet the Systems Corp people tomorrow at 5.</br></br>"}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}